<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="connection"><span aria-hidden="true">01</span>Trace the actual connection</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Start at the computer and follow the path to the display. Write down the laptop model, dock model, monitor model, charger and cable types. Check which device supplies power and which device carries the display signal.</p><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">The same connector shape can support different capabilities. A cable may fit while failing to carry video, provide enough charging power or support the display mode you want. Check the manufacturers' documentation for the exact combination before buying an adapter or replacement cable.</p><ul class="mb-6 list-disc space-y-3 pl-6 text-muted"><li>Confirm the monitor is powered on and set to the matching input.</li><li>Check that the dock has its own required power connection.</li><li>Look for loose, damaged or sharply bent cables.</li><li>Keep the computer, dock and display ventilated.</li></ul>
<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="display"><span aria-hidden="true">02</span>Set the screen arrangement</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">On Windows 11, open Settings, then System and Display. Use Identify to match the on-screen numbers to the physical monitors. Arrange the display icons to match their positions, apply the change and move the pointer across the boundary.</p><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Duplicate and extend are different choices. Duplicate shows the same content on each display. Extend creates a larger workspace so windows can be placed on separate screens. Choose the mode that matches the task rather than assuming a second monitor is automatically configured.</p><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">On a Mac, use the display controls and instructions for the specific Mac, dock and monitor combination. Do not apply Windows steps to a Mac system.</p><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Source: <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/hardware/display-graphics/how-to-use-multiple-monitors-in-windows">Microsoft support: use multiple monitors in Windows</a>.</p>
<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="safe-test"><span aria-hidden="true">03</span>Test without creating a second problem</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Save your work before disconnecting anything. Make one reversible change, such as reseating one cable or selecting the correct input, then check the result. If the result changes, record what changed before continuing.</p><div class="mb-8 overflow-x-auto" role="region" aria-label="Home Office Setup reference" tabindex="0"><table role="table" class="w-full border-collapse text-left text-sm md:text-base"><thead><tr><th scope="col" class="border border-line bg-surface p-4 font-bold text-ink">Observation</th><th scope="col" class="border border-line bg-surface p-4 font-bold text-ink">Next bounded check</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label="Observation" class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">No picture</td><td data-label="Next bounded check" class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">Check power, selected input and whether the path supports video.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Observation" class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">Picture but no charging</td><td data-label="Next bounded check" class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">Check the dock power arrangement and the documented charging capability.</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Observation" class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">Screens appear in the wrong order</td><td data-label="Next bounded check" class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">Use Identify and arrange the display icons to match the desk.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Avoid opening equipment, bypassing security controls or starting a firmware update as a first troubleshooting step. Keep the original arrangement if the result is unclear.</p>
